From f08727d1116df20191bb2327ef7faa28e27691f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:10:05 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] CUDA: fold the residual add into the following
 rms_norm+mul

Port of the R9700/HIP track patch 0008 ("CUDA/HIP: fold the residual add into
the following rms_norm+mul", Claude Fable 5), unchanged: shared ggml-cuda
code with no architecture-gated paths. One kernel produces the add result,
stores it exactly as the (possibly multi-add fused) add would, and then
normalises the values it just wrote with the stock rms_norm_f32 statements.

GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_PRE_ADD_NORM=1 disables the optimization.
